{"genre": "Essay", "passage_A": "French historian Fernand Braudel significantly contributed to the Annales school of history by challenging traditional historical methods through his focus on long-term perspectives. Braudel believed in examining history across various time scales, from the immediate political and social events of daily life to broader geographical, social, and economic factors that influence historical change over centuries.

