{"genre": "Essay", "passage_A": "One of the key reasons why an effective organizational structure is crucial for budgetary control lies in its impact on communication and decision-making processes. A well-thought-out structure defines reporting lines and clearly delineates responsibilities and authorities, which fosters efficient coordination and collaboration. This clarity ensures that everyone within the organization understands and adheres to budgetary constraints.

